# Winning a travel encounter mid-journey resumes the walk with the world in view.
#
# The victory branch wiped the fight screen with a bare Clear, which paints every cell opaque black,
# and Traveling draws nothing but its progress box: the rest of the journey was walked over a black
# screen, the box floating on it, until the arrival repainted. A playtester met it on the first
# bandit; no script did, because every script switches the random rolls off and the two staged
# encounters (--encounter-on-arrival, --start-fight) take the other two branches.
#
# --encounter-mid-journey stages this one. `inspect overlay` is the assertion: `dump` cannot tell an
# opaque-black blank from a transparent one. The port is the one place of its name in reach at seed
# 42, more than a step away; the walk is left to finish, and its arrival is the second half.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --encounter-mid-journey wolf

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60

# Before setting out: the world map is the reference.
expect-state overlay "world=shown"

travel port
travel-go

wait mode EncounterPrompt 90
click engage
wait mode Fighting 90
fight-end victory

# The journey resumes and ends where it was going. Under --playground the rest of the walk takes no
# time at all, so the reading is the one taken as Traveling was entered — after the fight, since the
# entry before it is overwritten: the world behind the progress box, not a black sheet.
wait mode LocationInteraction 120
expect-state overlay "overlay-entry Traveling world=shown"
quit
